# Line endings, decided here rather than by whoever clones.
#
# This repo is edited on Windows and runs on Linux. `core.autocrlf=true` on the
# editing machine happens to store LF today, but it is a per-machine setting and
# the next contributor's may differ — and a shell script that reaches a VPS with
# CRLF fails as `bash: $'\r': command not found`, which names neither the file
# nor the reason. So the files that a shell, systemd or Node has to execute are
# pinned to LF in the repo *and* in every working tree.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
*.js            text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf

# The mail fixture is normalised like everything else, deliberately. RFC 5322 is
# CRLF and a real DKIM signature is computed over it — but this fixture's `b=` is
# scrubbed to XXXX, so nothing verifies it cryptographically and the parser reads
# either form. Checked: `paysvc/test/alert.test.js` passes against the LF copy.
*.eml           text eol=lf
